{
  "id": "COMPOUND:34310 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Jasmonic acid appears to interact with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of target relationships, suggesting a potential mechanism involving multiple pathways. The evidence indicates that (+)-Jasmonic acid acts as a target for VMRC-LCP and SNB-78, which in turn are targets of 1,2-Dihydroheudelotinol and Cocosamide B, respectively. These compounds all ultimately lead to the Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The integration of these pathways suggests that (+)-Jasmonic acid may influence the activity of these intermediates, which then modulate the replication process of the target protein. The presence of multiple targets and the shared downstream effect on Replicase polyprotein 1ab imply a complex regulatory network, possibly involving metabolic or signaling pathways that are not fully elucidated. The evidence supports a role for (+)-Jasmonic acid in modulating the replication machinery, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully characterized.",
